			       ------------------
			    OfficeFloor Migration Guide
			       ------------------
			      Daniel Sagenschneider
			       ------------------

OfficeFloor Migration Guide

  This guide is for those interested in progressively migrating from a Spring Boot application to
  running natively on OfficeFloor.  The {{{./index.html}Tutorials}} page covers adding OfficeFloor
  capabilities to Spring Boot without any migration.  Come back here only if you want to go further.

  The migration is structured as progressive stages.  You can stop at any stage.

  [[1]] <<Spring in OfficeFloor>> hosts your Spring beans inside the OfficeFloor runtime.  All
        existing Spring configuration continues to work.  Existing Spring Web MVC controllers
        continue to function while YAML REST procedures are added alongside them.

  [[2]] <<Native OfficeFloor>> removes the Spring dependency entirely.  All REST YAML files,
        service classes, and team configurations carry over unchanged.

  []

  Additional content covering reactive streams, cloud deployment, and legacy integration is
  included below for completeness.


* Phase 1: Spring in OfficeFloor

  In this phase the OfficeFloor runtime takes ownership of the HTTP server while your existing
  Spring configuration continues to supply dependency-injected beans.  No Spring code changes are
  required.  Moving to this phase unlocks further OfficeFloor capabilities such as native thread
  injection and the full WoOF infrastructure layer, while the familiar Spring programming model
  remains intact.


** Spring Beans

  Host Spring beans directly as OfficeFloor managed objects.  Your Spring <<<@Service>>>,
  <<<@Repository>>>, and <<<@Component>>> beans are available for injection into any OfficeFloor
  procedure exactly as they are in a Spring Boot application.

*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
|| Tutorial                                                    || Description                                               || Covered
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./spring-officefloor/SpringHttpServer/index.html}Spring Beans}} | Host Spring beans inside the OfficeFloor runtime. Spring is used purely as a dependency supplier; all beans remain available for injection. | SpringSupplierSource\
|                                                              |                                                            | Spring beans as managed objects
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+


** Spring Web MVC in OfficeFloor

  Host an existing Spring Web MVC application inside the OfficeFloor runtime.  Existing
  <<<@Controller>>> endpoints continue to work while YAML REST procedures can be added alongside
  them.

*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
|| Tutorial                                                    || Description                                               || Covered
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./spring-officefloor/SpringWebMvcHttpServer/index.html}Spring Web MVC}} | Run Spring Web MVC @Controller endpoints within OfficeFloor while adding YAML REST procedures. | Spring Web MVC\
|                                                              |                                                            | @Controller in OfficeFloor
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+


** Spring WebFlux in OfficeFloor

  Host existing Spring WebFlux <<<@RestController>>> components within the OfficeFloor runtime.
  Spring MVC natively supports <<<Mono\<T\>>>> and <<<Flux\<T\>>>> return types, and Java 21
  Virtual Threads provide the non-blocking throughput that WebFlux was designed for — so existing
  reactive controller code runs unchanged without migrating to the Spring MVC programming model.

*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
|| Tutorial                                                    || Description                                               || Covered
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./spring-officefloor/SpringWebFluxHttpServer/index.html}Spring WebFlux}} | Host Spring WebFlux @RestController components returning Mono/Flux within the OfficeFloor runtime alongside YAML REST procedures. | Spring WebFlux\
|                                                              |                                                            | Mono / Flux in OfficeFloor\
|                                                              |                                                            | Virtual Threads
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+


* Phase 2: Native OfficeFloor

  If there is interest in removing Spring as a runtime dependency, OfficeFloor can run without it.
  All REST YAML files, service classes, and team configurations carry over unchanged.  The following
  tutorials explore the complete set of native OfficeFloor capabilities organised by concern.


** Core REST and Dependency Injection

  The foundation tutorials for native OfficeFloor REST applications.

*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
|| Tutorial                                                    || Description                                               || Covered
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./native/native-core/RestHttpServer/index.html}REST}}            | Declare REST endpoints as YAML configuration; dependency inject request data and services. | REST\
|                                                              |                                                            | @PathParameter , HttpException
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./native/native-core/DiPojoHttpServer/index.html}Dependency Injection}} | Dependency inject plain old Java objects (POJOs) into REST procedures. | Dependency Injection
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./native/native-core/EnvironmentHttpServer/index.html}Environment}} | Configure application behaviour across environments using properties and profiles. | @Property , Profile
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./native/native-core/LoggerHttpServer/index.html}Logging}}       | Inject loggers that identify their location within the application. | Logger
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./native/native-core/SwaggerHttpServer/index.html}OpenAPI / Swagger}} | Generate OpenAPI documentation from native OfficeFloor REST YAML endpoint declarations. | {{{https://www.openapis.org/}OpenAPI}}\
|                                                              |                                                            | {{{https://swagger.io/}Swagger}}
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+
| {{{./native/native-core/ExceptionHttpServer/index.html}Exception Handling}} | Handle and map exceptions within native OfficeFloor REST flows. | @Parameter\
|                                                              |                                                            | Exception handling
*--------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------+


